19:45.780 --> 19:48.480
Look for the figures of the three musketeers on the big

19:48.480 --> 19:49.480
white wrapper.

19:49.480 --> 19:52.680
The biggest nickels worth of chocolate covered candy in

19:52.680 --> 19:53.780
America.

19:53.780 --> 19:55.780
Three musketeers!

19:55.780 --> 20:04.780
And now boys and girls, once again back to the main arena.

20:04.780 --> 20:07.080
And in case you weren't tuned in earlier on the show here,

20:07.080 --> 20:09.380
once again is our guest trainer of the menagerie.

20:09.380 --> 20:12.380
He's bringing back five wonderful animals to our

20:12.380 --> 20:13.780
program at this point.

20:13.780 --> 20:14.980
So here he is, Homer F.

20:14.980 --> 20:23.180
Snow from Snow Sealatoria.

20:23.180 --> 20:35.880
Now first of all we're going to meet Nikki, Cindy, and Sandy.

20:35.880 --> 20:46.880
Now everybody say their prayers.

20:46.880 --> 20:49.480
And now boys and girls, you're going to see the cutest little

20:49.480 --> 20:52.380
animal we've ever seen on Super Circus.

20:52.380 --> 20:55.580
Here he is, Penny the Penguin.

20:55.580 --> 20:58.080
He's nine years old but we still don't know whether he's a

20:58.080 --> 20:58.780
boy or girl.

20:58.780 --> 21:00.580
He's never laid an egg yet.

21:00.580 --> 21:03.180
We don't want him to lay one on our program today either.

21:03.180 --> 21:04.680
Oh, he's a jumping penguin.

21:04.680 --> 21:05.280
Watch this.

21:05.280 --> 21:06.180
He's a jumper.

21:06.180 --> 21:06.980
Up and up.

21:06.980 --> 21:10.980
Oh, what a fine way to jump.

21:10.980 --> 21:14.480
Well, anyway, there he gets a little pat from his buddies.

21:14.480 --> 21:20.180
And there he is, Penny the Penguin.

21:20.180 --> 21:25.180
Back in your igloo, buddy, because next up we're going to

21:25.180 --> 21:28.880
see Cindy and she'll show you how to roll the barrel.

21:28.880 --> 21:54.280
She shows off her remarkable talent.

21:54.280 --> 21:55.480
Now she rolls the barrel.

21:55.480 --> 22:00.180
Trying to pass the buck, I mean the ball.

22:00.180 --> 22:08.180
Now she rolls the barrel and passes the ball back.

22:08.180 --> 22:12.580
Now here comes Sandy, boys and girls.

22:12.580 --> 22:13.880
You just never know what he's going to do.

22:13.880 --> 22:19.380
He's a clown.

22:19.380 --> 22:22.680
Sandy's a clown and it's just like having Scampi come on the

22:22.680 --> 22:23.180
stage.

22:23.180 --> 22:25.180
You just never know what's going to happen.

22:25.180 --> 22:27.880
Let's see if he can throw that ring back to his trainer,

22:27.880 --> 22:28.680
Homer F. Snow.

22:28.680 --> 22:31.680
Back to the – oh, Sandy.

22:31.680 --> 22:32.480
Now look here.

22:32.480 --> 22:33.680
You better do what you told her.

22:33.680 --> 22:36.180
You're going to get a cut of 50% in salary.

22:36.180 --> 22:38.680
Now you just go right over there and pick up that white ball and

22:38.680 --> 22:40.780
take it back to your seat.

22:40.780 --> 22:42.380
Ah-ha.

22:42.380 --> 22:44.380
Okay, young fella, you redeemed yourself.

22:44.380 --> 23:03.880
Now it's time for baseball.

23:03.880 --> 23:06.280
The boys throw the ball around a little bit.

23:06.280 --> 23:07.780
There we are.

23:07.780 --> 23:08.980
Ball's at first base.

23:08.980 --> 23:10.180
Let's get it over to second, boys.

23:10.180 --> 23:12.180
That's right.

23:12.180 --> 23:13.780
Got a man on base after that one.

23:13.780 --> 23:15.480
He's over in second.

23:15.480 --> 23:18.880
Sandy, if we don't watch out, we'll have a great big score up

23:18.880 --> 23:23.280
against the Seals team.

23:23.280 --> 23:23.880
There we go.

23:23.880 --> 23:25.080
Now back to home plate.

23:25.080 --> 23:37.080
Hey, the runner's out and the Seals win the game.

23:37.080 --> 23:39.880
Sandy now again shows us how it's supposed to be done.

23:39.880 --> 24:04.480
Still balancing at its very best.

24:04.480 --> 24:14.080
Now it's time for juggling as all three of them.

24:14.080 --> 24:19.980
Juggle the baton.

24:19.980 --> 24:23.780
There's Nicky, passing it to Cindy, and there it is to Sandy.

24:23.780 --> 24:25.480
Oh, pretty fancy, huh?

24:25.480 --> 24:26.680
Whoops.

24:26.680 --> 24:30.780
Looks like Sandy wins.

24:30.780 --> 24:38.880
Yeah.

24:38.880 --> 24:40.280
Now here comes Nicky.

24:40.280 --> 24:43.780
No relation to the clown of the same name.

24:43.780 --> 24:45.880
Oh, they don't even look alike.

24:45.880 --> 24:49.080
But he takes the center spotlight for a Seals hot dog.

24:49.080 --> 25:00.980
♪♪

25:00.980 --> 25:04.580
Say, Homer, I understand that Nicky wants to be a TV actor.

25:04.580 --> 25:12.180
Let's see how well he works in front of the camera, huh?

25:12.180 --> 25:14.780
Pretty good, huh, kids?

25:14.780 --> 25:18.980
Very good.

25:18.980 --> 25:22.880
Well, that's very good, but how about some serious dramatics?

25:22.880 --> 25:25.580
Ah, I see that Homer is going to play the part of a fisherman.

25:25.580 --> 25:29.080
Seals hate fishermen, so he's going to take a shot at Nicky.

25:29.080 --> 25:31.680
Oh, gee.

25:31.680 --> 25:33.380
Where'd you hit him, Homer?

25:33.380 --> 25:36.880
Huh?

25:36.880 --> 25:38.680
In the flipper?

25:38.680 --> 25:40.580
Aw.

25:40.580 --> 25:44.780
Say, Homer, just what would happen if Nicky got hit in the flipper

25:44.780 --> 25:49.080
and he only had three left?

25:49.080 --> 25:54.680
♪♪

25:54.680 --> 25:59.880
Ha ha.

25:59.880 --> 26:02.980
And now, boy, hey, look what's coming on the stage now.

26:02.980 --> 26:04.280
Did you see that?

26:04.280 --> 26:09.680
This is Perry the Pelican, the world's only and first-trained pelican, boys and girls.

26:09.680 --> 26:12.280
Watch him, watch Homer put him through his paces.

26:12.280 --> 26:14.980
He wants to get acquainted a little bit with the super circus set.

26:14.980 --> 26:16.580
Yes, hooray.

26:16.580 --> 26:18.080
Up you go, my friend.

26:18.080 --> 26:19.380
Ha ha.

26:19.380 --> 26:23.280
Oh, he's got a tremendous wingspread there, kids, about six and a half feet.

26:23.280 --> 26:25.280
Now watch.

26:25.280 --> 26:31.180
He does exactly what Homer tells him to.

26:31.180 --> 26:33.380
Ho ho ho, chow down, huh?

26:33.380 --> 26:36.080
He sure can get rid of that fish, I tell you.

26:36.080 --> 26:39.280
Say, Homer, does he ever miss catching a fish?

26:39.280 --> 26:43.280
I don't know how he could really ever miss, Kirshner, I really don't.

26:43.280 --> 26:44.280
Why not?

26:44.280 --> 26:45.280
You want to show us?

26:45.280 --> 26:47.280
Yeah, look here, he's got a regular catcher's mitt here.

26:47.280 --> 26:50.780
Oh, ha ha ha ha ha.

26:50.780 --> 26:54.080
No, sir, don't let him mistake my nose for a fish, no sirree.

26:54.080 --> 26:55.180
He's a nice guy, though.

26:55.180 --> 26:56.180
He is.

26:56.180 --> 26:57.180
He really, he likes to neck.

26:57.180 --> 26:59.280
Let's do a little necking with him here.

26:59.280 --> 27:05.480
He's a little nervous about Mike, and we'll try to make him love you.

27:05.480 --> 27:10.680
He says, yo, yo.

27:10.680 --> 27:12.880
Well, I think he'd like to do a little trick here, roll the barrel out.

27:12.880 --> 27:13.380
How about it?

27:13.380 --> 27:14.480
He would like to roll the barrel?

27:14.480 --> 27:16.380
You mean he can roll the barrel just like the seals can?

27:16.380 --> 27:17.380
Oh, sure, make the seals jealous.

27:17.380 --> 27:20.880
Oh, gee, well, all right, let's make the seals a little jealous.

27:20.880 --> 27:23.380
Here's Perry the pelican for us, girls.

27:23.380 --> 27:25.380
Rolling out the barrel.

27:25.380 --> 27:50.380
♪♪

27:50.380 --> 27:53.380
Penny the penguin, Perry the pelican, and those wonderful seals.

27:53.380 --> 27:55.880
Come out, now, Mary Hartline, Barney Scanty, Patton Clifford,

27:55.880 --> 27:57.380
and Nicky Trent.

27:57.380 --> 28:00.380
Gather around the old ringmaster, because we have to say goodbye

28:00.380 --> 28:04.380
to all these wonderful people.

28:04.380 --> 28:08.380
And goodbye from Snickers, everybody's favorite candy bar,

28:08.380 --> 28:13.380
especially mine.

28:13.380 --> 28:19.380
Free Mascoteers, the biggest Snickers worth of chocolate-covered candy

28:19.380 --> 28:21.380
in America.

28:21.380 --> 28:25.380
Now, kids, you can get both Snickers and Free Mascoteers in the Sixers pack.

28:25.380 --> 28:28.380
Six delicious candy bars in one handy carton.

28:28.380 --> 28:31.380
Get either Snickers Sixers or Free Mascoteers Sixers,

28:31.380 --> 28:35.380
and say, they're both great chilled or frozen.

28:35.380 --> 28:37.380
Say, boys and girls, here once again are our wonderful aerialists,

28:37.380 --> 28:39.380
Les Geraldos.

28:39.380 --> 28:41.380
Come on out.

28:41.380 --> 28:43.380
And here's Homer F. Snow.

28:43.380 --> 28:44.380
Let's see who he comes out with.

28:44.380 --> 28:46.380
And Homer, you got an animal ready that he can show us?

28:46.380 --> 28:48.380
Good, here he comes.

28:48.380 --> 28:51.380
Oh, well, well, well.

28:51.380 --> 28:52.380
There's Nicky the Clown.

28:52.380 --> 28:54.380
Boys and girls, that's it for the Midwest issue of TV Guide

28:54.380 --> 28:56.380
for a story about our wonderful clowns.

28:56.380 --> 28:59.380
Now, until next week, this is Claude Kirschner saying,

28:59.380 --> 29:01.380
bye-bye, everybody.

29:01.380 --> 29:03.380
♪♪

